1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,240
Imagine a strange object crossing the night sky.

2
00:00:03,240 --> 00:00:05,960
It shines like the sun beside the moon.

3
00:00:05,960 --> 00:00:10,000
It moves like a bird, but no one recognizes its shape.

4
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:12,840
A red vapor hangs in the clouds,

5
00:00:12,840 --> 00:00:15,840
or a blue flame falls like fire.

6
00:00:15,840 --> 00:00:19,480
Centuries before the word UFO existed.

7
00:00:19,480 --> 00:00:22,160
Josayon court scribes recorded these events

8
00:00:22,160 --> 00:00:24,360
in official state documents.

9
00:00:24,360 --> 00:00:27,680
Were they comets, auroras, meteors,

10
00:00:27,680 --> 00:00:30,240
or astronomical illusions?

11
00:00:30,240 --> 00:00:32,880
Or did the Josayon annals preserve encounters

12
00:00:32,880 --> 00:00:36,320
with something that still has no name?

13
00:00:36,320 --> 00:00:40,320
The Josayon annals, known in Korean as the Josian Wang

14
00:00:40,320 --> 00:00:43,400
Jo Silok, were the official daily records

15
00:00:43,400 --> 00:00:45,440
of the Josian dynasty.

16
00:00:45,440 --> 00:00:48,000
They were not tabloids or myths.

17
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:51,520
They were state documents written by professional historians

18
00:00:51,520 --> 00:00:55,320
who recorded what happened at court, what officials reported,

19
00:00:55,320 --> 00:00:58,960
and what the heavens supposedly revealed.

20
00:00:58,960 --> 00:01:03,880
In Josayon political culture, the sky was never just scenery.

21
00:01:03,880 --> 00:01:07,960
Celestial anomalies were treated as signs from heaven.

22
00:01:07,960 --> 00:01:11,520
A strange light could mean the king's virtue had failed.

23
00:01:11,520 --> 00:01:13,600
A minister had acted corruptly,

24
00:01:13,600 --> 00:01:16,680
or the dynasty's fate was turning.

25
00:01:16,680 --> 00:01:19,400
Because of that belief, astronomical events

26
00:01:19,400 --> 00:01:22,400
were written down with unusual care.

27
00:01:22,400 --> 00:01:24,440
The color of a vapor,

28
00:01:24,440 --> 00:01:27,120
whether it moved east or west,

29
00:01:27,120 --> 00:01:31,000
whether it orbited the moon or vanished in an instant,

30
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:36,040
whether it looked like a bell, a bird, a dragon, or a flame.

31
00:01:36,040 --> 00:01:38,800
Modern readers often translate these descriptions

32
00:01:38,800 --> 00:01:41,080
into UFO sightings.

33
00:01:41,080 --> 00:01:44,920
But the Josayon scribes themselves did not have that word.

34
00:01:44,920 --> 00:01:48,600
They had astronomy, omens, and a state ideology

35
00:01:48,600 --> 00:01:52,680
that made the heavens politically important.

36
00:01:52,680 --> 00:01:54,720
2130.

37
00:01:54,720 --> 00:01:58,640
Four Heaven Quack, the records begin.

38
00:01:58,640 --> 00:02:02,400
The earliest strange sky reports appear across the annals

39
00:02:02,400 --> 00:02:04,320
with surprising frequency.

40
00:02:04,320 --> 00:02:09,400
Some were interpreted as comets, others as auspicious signs.

41
00:02:09,400 --> 00:02:13,200
A few were alarming enough to trigger official discussions.

42
00:02:13,200 --> 00:02:16,840
In several entries, scribes described red vapors

43
00:02:16,840 --> 00:02:20,120
and fire-like lights that appeared in the night sky.

44
00:02:20,120 --> 00:02:22,080
Some resembled pillars.

45
00:02:22,080 --> 00:02:24,640
Others spread like banners.

46
00:02:24,640 --> 00:02:27,560
Because these phenomena were treated as warnings,

47
00:02:27,560 --> 00:02:31,320
the court often responded with rituals, court discussions,

48
00:02:31,320 --> 00:02:35,680
or orders for officials to reflect on their conduct.

49
00:02:35,680 --> 00:02:38,960
Other descriptions sounded even stranger.

50
00:02:38,960 --> 00:02:41,960
A bright object appeared near the moon.

51
00:02:41,960 --> 00:02:45,960
A light moved across the sky with the speed of an arrow.

52
00:02:45,960 --> 00:02:50,920
An object descended, changed, shape, and vanished.

53
00:02:50,920 --> 00:02:55,360
In court language, such events were recorded as strange chi,

54
00:02:55,360 --> 00:03:01,000
unprecedented events, or objects that had never been seen before.

55
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:04,840
This is where the UFO interpretation begins.

56
00:03:04,840 --> 00:03:08,480
A modern reader sees a glowing object, motion,

57
00:03:08,480 --> 00:03:12,480
and an explicit statement that nobody recognized it.

58
00:03:12,480 --> 00:03:16,000
A Josayon reader saw a sign from heaven.

59
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:19,760
The same event could therefore serve two mysteries at once,

60
00:03:19,760 --> 00:03:24,640
a mystery of astronomy and a mystery of politics.

61
00:03:24,640 --> 00:03:32,040
Dirted cock, seven go, the weird details.

62
00:03:32,040 --> 00:03:34,360
What makes these records so compelling

63
00:03:34,360 --> 00:03:36,960
is not just that lights appeared.

64
00:03:36,960 --> 00:03:40,200
It is the details preserved by the scribes.

65
00:03:40,200 --> 00:03:43,920
Some objects were described as hanging in the sky like a bell.

66
00:03:43,920 --> 00:03:46,200
Some moved against the wind.

67
00:03:46,320 --> 00:03:50,280
Some seemed to split apart or shine in multiple colors.

68
00:03:50,280 --> 00:03:55,040
Some were said to resemble dragons, birds, or wheels.

69
00:03:55,040 --> 00:03:57,920
A few reports described a light descending low enough

70
00:03:57,920 --> 00:04:00,600
that people on the ground could see its shape clearly

71
00:04:00,600 --> 00:04:02,560
before it disappeared.

72
00:04:02,560 --> 00:04:05,880
The annals also preserved the emotional response.

73
00:04:05,880 --> 00:04:07,920
Courteers were frightened.

74
00:04:07,920 --> 00:04:10,320
The king asked for explanations.

75
00:04:10,320 --> 00:04:12,680
Astronomers were consulted.

76
00:04:12,680 --> 00:04:15,240
In some cases, the court treated the appearance

77
00:04:15,240 --> 00:04:19,080
as proof that heaven was dissatisfied with the ruler.

78
00:04:19,080 --> 00:04:21,840
That political layer is crucial.

79
00:04:21,840 --> 00:04:26,520
If a comet appeared, it was not merely an astronomical object.

80
00:04:26,520 --> 00:04:28,080
It was a message.

81
00:04:28,080 --> 00:04:30,880
If a strange vapor crossed the sky,

82
00:04:30,880 --> 00:04:34,360
the king might be pressured to reform his government.

83
00:04:34,360 --> 00:04:39,440
The heavens were, in effect, part of the political feedback system.

84
00:04:39,440 --> 00:04:44,280
Seen this way, a UFO siding in the Josayon annals

85
00:04:44,280 --> 00:04:46,880
is also a record of anxiety.

86
00:04:46,880 --> 00:04:49,760
Every unexplained sign became evidence

87
00:04:49,760 --> 00:04:53,160
that something in the kingdom was out of balance.

88
00:04:53,160 --> 00:04:58,120
Modern UFO researchers often point to three explanations.

89
00:04:58,120 --> 00:05:00,880
First, natural phenomena.

90
00:05:00,880 --> 00:05:05,880
Comets, meteors, fireballs, atmospheric reflections,

91
00:05:05,880 --> 00:05:08,920
and rare auroras could easily produce

92
00:05:08,920 --> 00:05:11,440
the reported shapes and colors.

93
00:05:11,440 --> 00:05:14,440
Josayon's scribes lacked modern astronomy,

94
00:05:14,440 --> 00:05:16,720
but they were careful observers.

95
00:05:16,720 --> 00:05:21,720
Their language, fire, vapor, light, bells, birds.

96
00:05:23,880 --> 00:05:26,080
Sounds exactly like what people write

97
00:05:26,080 --> 00:05:30,040
when they are describing something real but unfamiliar.

98
00:05:30,040 --> 00:05:33,360
Second, misidentification.

99
00:05:33,360 --> 00:05:37,160
Bright planets, the moon through clouds, weather balloons

100
00:05:37,160 --> 00:05:39,760
and military signals have all been reported

101
00:05:39,760 --> 00:05:43,000
as strange objects in every era.

102
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:46,920
In the 17th or 18th century, a high-altitude lantern

103
00:05:46,920 --> 00:05:49,360
or a fast-moving weather phenomenon

104
00:05:49,360 --> 00:05:52,040
could have become a palace mystery.

105
00:05:52,040 --> 00:05:54,880
Third, cultural framing.

106
00:05:54,880 --> 00:05:58,880
The annals were written inside a confusion worldview.

107
00:05:58,880 --> 00:06:03,880
If the king ruled badly, heaven warned him through the sky.

108
00:06:03,880 --> 00:06:06,920
That does not mean the reports were fabricated.

109
00:06:06,920 --> 00:06:10,040
It means the scribes selected and interpreted events

110
00:06:10,040 --> 00:06:12,680
through a political cosmology.

111
00:06:12,680 --> 00:06:16,160
A natural event could be real while its official meaning

112
00:06:16,160 --> 00:06:18,920
was shaped by ideology.

113
00:06:18,920 --> 00:06:21,400
There is a fourth possibility, of course,

114
00:06:21,400 --> 00:06:24,880
that some observations were genuinely anomalous,

115
00:06:24,880 --> 00:06:28,680
but anomaly is not proof of an alien spacecraft.

116
00:06:28,680 --> 00:06:30,800
A record without physical evidence,

117
00:06:30,800 --> 00:06:32,920
multiple independent measurements,

118
00:06:32,920 --> 00:06:37,400
or a recoverable object, cannot settle the question.

119
00:06:37,400 --> 00:06:42,040
What the Josian annals prove is narrower and more interesting.

120
00:06:42,040 --> 00:06:46,400
Pre-modern Koreans saw things in the sky they could not explain

121
00:06:46,400 --> 00:06:49,320
and their state considered those things important enough

122
00:06:49,320 --> 00:06:52,520
to preserve, so the Josian annals may not

123
00:06:52,520 --> 00:06:55,560
prove the existence of UFOs.

124
00:06:55,560 --> 00:06:58,200
But they do prove something else.

125
00:06:58,200 --> 00:07:01,200
Long before the modern flying saucer era,

126
00:07:01,200 --> 00:07:03,280
Korean officials were watching the sky

127
00:07:03,280 --> 00:07:05,800
with extraordinary seriousness.

128
00:07:05,800 --> 00:07:09,600
They recorded color, movement, direction, and shape.

129
00:07:09,600 --> 00:07:11,240
They debated meaning.

130
00:07:11,240 --> 00:07:13,880
They worried that the heavens were speaking,

131
00:07:13,880 --> 00:07:16,480
and they left those worries in the official history

132
00:07:16,480 --> 00:07:17,920
of a dynasty.

133
00:07:17,920 --> 00:07:20,000
Maybe those lights were comets.

134
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:22,560
Maybe they were atmospheric fire.

135
00:07:22,560 --> 00:07:25,800
Maybe they were something even stranger.

136
00:07:25,800 --> 00:07:30,960
The most enduring mystery may not be what crossed the Josian sky.

137
00:07:30,960 --> 00:07:33,360
It may be that a civilization wrote down

138
00:07:33,360 --> 00:07:36,840
its fear of the heavens, preserved it for centuries,

139
00:07:36,840 --> 00:07:40,040
and handed it to us as a record.

140
00:07:40,040 --> 00:07:42,520
If you found this story fascinating,

141
00:07:42,520 --> 00:07:45,760
subscribe for more Korean mysteries.

142
00:07:45,760 --> 00:07:49,280
The Josian annals contain many more unexplained records

143
00:07:49,280 --> 00:07:51,800
waiting to be translated for the world.

144
00:07:51,800 --> 00:07:53,480
And hit that like button.

145
00:07:53,480 --> 00:07:56,600
It helps more people discover these forgotten stories.

